  "body": "The spec for document.open reads like the resulting document gets its baseURI copied from the opened document, however, that's not the behavior I observe in Blink.\n\nLooking at the source of Blink, it's unclear to me what it's actually trying to do. I wonder what Gecko does, and would like the document.open spec to be updated to reflect what actually happens.\n\nHere's what happens in Blink: in a document of https://example.test I think the following script should show an alert \"about:blank\" but it actually alerts https://example.test\n\nvar ifr = document.createElement(\"iframe\");\nifr.src = \"about:blank\"\ndocument.body.appendChild(ifr);\nifr.contentDocument.open();\nalert(ifr.contentDocument.baseURI)\n\n@bzbarsky @foolip \n",
